e_of_purples","wavelength_nm":null},{"index":10,"type":"line_of_purples","wavelength_nm":null},{"index":11,"type":"line_of_purples","wavelength_nm":null}]},"MONOCHROMATIC_WAVELENGTH_DIAGNOSTIC":{"definition":"dominant-wavelength status of boundary projection","result":"NOT_A_COMPLETE_12_CYCLE","reason":"indices 9–11 fall on the line of purples and have no single monochromatic wavelength"}},"soundAdapter":{"source":{"C":0.0,"D":0.16992500144231237,"E":0.32192809488736235,"F":0.41503749927884376,"G":0.5849625007211562,"A":0.7369655941662062,"B":0.9068905956085185,"C8":1.0},"fixedSlots":{"C":0,"D":2,"E":4,"F":5,"G":7,"A":9,"B":11,"C8":12},"status":"Declared just-intonation-to-color-position comparison, not physical identity"},"residualReplays":[{"carrier":"RYB_EQUAL12_HISTORICAL","score":0.16292953955681744,"reportedScore":0.16292953955681744,"sourceMetric":"(1/3)*sum12*abs(soundPosition-colorPosition[fixedSlot])","signedResiduals":{"C":0.0,"D":0.003258334775645716,"E":-0.011405238445970967,"F":-0.0016291673878229274,"G":0.0016291673878228163,"A":-0.013034405833793783,"B":-0.00977607105814815,"C8":0.0},"replayed":true},{"carrier":"LINEAR_sRGB_CIE1931_xy_HUE","score":1.0107803346483477,"reportedScore":1.010780334648348,"sourceMetric":"(1/3)*sum12*abs(soundPosition-colorPosition[fixedSlot])","signedResiduals":{"C":0.0,"D":0.006986047442312376,"E":0.06496125988736234,"F":0.06819934927884375,"G":-0.021695399278843785,"A":0.03080058216620618,"B":0.06005244560851852,"C8":0.0},"replayed":true},{"carrier":"LINEAR_sRGB_CIE1976_uv_HUE","score":0.5426571257801993,"reportedScore":0.5426571257801993,"sourceMetric":"(1/3)*sum12*abs(soundPosition-colorPosition[fixedSlot])","signedResiduals":{"C":0.0,"D":-0.03478963655768763,"E":0.0009893128873623702,"F":0.022547062278843732,"G":-0.035198650278843835,"A":-0.02773946083379375,"B":0.01440015860851851,"C8":0.0},"replayed":true},{"carrier":"LINEAR_sRGB_CIELAB_HUE","score":0.930246591549449,"reportedScore":0.930246591549449,"sourceMetric":"(1/3)*sum12*abs(soundPosition-colorPosition[fixedSlot])","signedResiduals":{"C":0.0,"D":-0.004669981557687636,"E":0.05522475188736237,"F":0.06967361327884375,"G":0.0008254747211562385,"A":-0.03618279083379383,"B":0.06598503560851843,"C8":0.0},"replayed":true},{"carrier":"CIE1931_BOUNDARY_PROJECTION_ARCLENGTH","score":1.2527253002483478,"reportedScore":1.252725300248348,"sourceMetric":"(1/3)*sum12*abs(soundPosition-colorPosition[fixedSlot])","signedResiduals":{"C":0.0,"D":0.03874480504231237,"E":0.10255604988736236,"F":0.04096210217884377,"G":-0.04629456577884383,"A":0.008201467566206211,"B":0.07642233460851844,"C8":0.0},"replayed":true}],"F_G_symmetry":{"colorSlotSumExact":"1","soundLogPositionSum":1,"consequence":"Opposite signed residuals are forced by the chosen complementary slots, not independent confirmation."},"monochromaticBoundary":{"fullClosed12WavelengthCycle":false,"nonspectralIndices":[9,10,11],"meaning":"Line-of-purples closure has no single monochromatic wavelength."},"infraUltra":{"recovered_decision":"Infrared and ultraviolet were treated as outside ordinary human color space and as parts of the larger EM possibility-space, not additional visible colors.","unresolved":"The retrieved pre-music record does not establish a finalized cross-scale mapping of IR/UV to infrasound/ultrasound or to ancestral SUN registers."},"laterPrimeEncoding":{"status":"LATER_NOT_ORIGINAL","mapping":{"R":2,"G":3,"B":5,"Y":6,"M":10,"C":15,"white":30,"black":1},"subtractive_example":"GCD(C=15,Y=6)=3 -> green","warning":"Do not treat this later deterministic encoding as the original color model."}},"stack":{"sourceHierarchy":["G0: abstract operator/geometry + boundary conditions","G1: normal modes / eigenmodes / field-mode spectrum","G2: time-dependent coupling, boundary or medium transition","G3: physical excitations (photons, phonons, hybrid quasiparticles, matter excitations)","G4: electromagnetic spectral power distribution","G5: retinal/cone projection","G6: opponent/contextual perceptual color"],"hypothesisUnderTest":"A pre-mechanical harmonic/modal geometry may be hierarchically prior to electromagnetic/visible-color realization. Established physics must first determine which transitions are already lawful and which claims remain unsupported.","sourceNoveltyLimits":["Determine whether frozen SUN relations select a specific operator geometry rather than merely generic spectral geometry.","Determine whether SUN predicts a lawful G1->G2 transition rule rather than borrowing a known parametric mechanism post hoc.","Test whether the old sound/color residuals disappear at the correct layer (spectrum, tristimulus, opponent representation) or persist.","Test whether a primordial hierarchy predicts any quantitative quantity not already forced by QFT or wave mechanics.","Define exactly what 'infra/ultra' means at each layer: outside observer band, outside carrier band, or ancestral/descendant register.","Do not make a cosmological causal claim until a distinct quantitative prediction separates SUN from generic time-dependent-field particle production."]},"vortex":{"sourceSpans":[{"sourcePath":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/HISTORICAL_MUSIC/ChatGPT-Mapping Primordials to Music-20261018-0133.md","lineStartOneBased":146,"lineEndOneBased":171,"quote":"## 3. The vortex: what it adds beyond the cylinder\n\nYour proposed vortex changes the architecture in a substantive way.\n\nThe earlier stack-of-dials model assumes a uniform state space at each tier. Your revised proposal instead introduces a family of potentially different state spaces:\n\n\\$$ \\mathcal X_0,\\mathcal X_1,\\mathcal X_2,\\ldots \\$$\n\nEach tier may have its own population, degrees of freedom, and available transformations.\n\nA candidate structure would be:\n\n\\$$ \\mathcal X_k=W\\_{72}\\times D_k \\$$\n\nwhere \\$D_k\\$ represents the additional state dimensions available at tier \\$k\\$.\n\nThe base-12 organization would be preserved as a recurring relational structure, while the full state space could expand.\n\nConceptual vortex: recurring twelvefold organization with tier-dependent capacity. Geometry is proposed, not derived from SUN.\n\nThis yields two independent questions:\n\n- Scale: How much larger is the next tier?\n- Dimension: What can the next tier represent or do that the previous tier cannot?\n\nAn exponentially expanding capacity might be modeled as \\$N_k=N_0b^k\\$, but the value of \\$b\\$, or whether exponential growth is appropriate at all, has not been established by the musical kernel.","sourceRole":"Historical conversational formulation; proposals/interpretations require their stated conditions and are not established geometry."},{"sourcePath":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/HISTORICAL_MUSIC/ChatGPT-Mapping Primordials to Music-20261018-0133.md","lineStartOneBased":239,"lineEndOneBased":260,"quote":"An internal operation has the form:\n\n\\$$ T_A:\\mathcal X_A\\rightarrow\\mathcal X_A \\$$\n\nA cross-class operation instead has the form:\n\n\\$$ \\boxed{ \\Phi\\_{A\\to B}:\\mathcal X_A\\rightarrow\\mathcal X_B } \\$$\n\nThe difference is that \\$\\Phi\\$ may change the type of state space, not merely a coordinate inside it.\n\nA useful transition contract would specify:\n\n- The source and destination classes, with their independently defined identities.\n- The initiating event and participating units, including joint parents or collective actors.\n- What persists: identities, relations, addresses, ordering, musical invariants, or historical lineage.\n- What changes: membership, dimensionality, permitted operations, boundaries, or observational scale.\n- Whether a reverse transition exists, and whether it is an actual inverse, a return path, or a different generative event.\n- The source evidence and mathematical obligations supporting each part.\n\nA cross-class operation need not be invertible. For example, an aggregation can preserve a collective while losing the information required to reconstruct every member from the aggregate alone.\n\nLikewise, a new dimension cannot be assumed to have a unique value inherited from the lower tier. It may require a new source-defined coordinate, a set of possible values, or an unresolved binding.","sourceRole":"Historical conversational formulation; proposals/interpretations require their stated conditions and are not established geometry."},{"sourcePath":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/HISTORICAL_MUSIC/ChatGPT-Mapping Primordials to Music-20261018-0133.md","lineStartOneBased":710,"lineEndOneBased":730,"quote":"Your research problem is to discover whether SUN's existing mathematics supplies a common structural description of these otherwise different transitions, without erasing their differences.\\\n\\\n\\## 3. What the vortex means in your explanation\\\n\\\nI now interpret the vortex primarily as a visualization of nested recurrence with changing scale and organizational rank.\\\n\\\nThe same musical relationships can recur at different levels, but the levels need not have identical contents or significance.\\\n\\\nThe tornado shape expresses your intuition that the structure is not simply a fixed stack of identical circular dials. It can expand in scope as generations accumulate, combine, or reorganize.\\\n\\\nYou are trying to visualize the relationship between:\\\n\\\n\\\\\\$$ \\text{recurrence} \\quad+\\quad \\text{scale} \\quad+\\quad \\text{generation} \\quad+\\quad \\text{class boundary}. \\\\\\$$\\\n\\\nYou are not necessarily asserting that the physical state space gains a new independent dimension at every octave.\\\n\\\nThat was an assumption I kept introducing.\\\n\\\nThe vortex remains a proposed geometric interpretation until its precise relationship to the existing SUN topology is demonstrated. But it is a legitimate way to communicate the question you're asking.\\\n\\\n\\## 4. What you're really asking about SUN's beginning\\","sourceRole":"Historical conversational formulation; proposals/interpretations require their stated conditions and are not established geometry."},{"sourcePath":"data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/HISTORICAL_MUSIC/ChatGPT-Mapping Primordials to Music-20261018-0133.md","lineStartOneBased":778,"lineEndOneBased":785,"quote":"Consider a piano or guitar: the same pitch class recurs across octaves, but its position and register change. Musical components can also combine into a new whole, such as a chord, which can itself become the reference for further musical construction. I'm interested in how these ideas relate to the existing SUN structure, without assuming that higher notes literally possess additional physical dimensions.\\\n\\\nI visualize the hierarchy as an expanding vortex rather than a uniform cylinder: recurring musical relationships across successive generations, potentially accompanied by changes in scope, organization, and available relationships.\\\n\\\nI want to determine where the first generation begins, using the Void/Silence distinction and tracing backward through the planetary, archonic, aeonic, and primordial structures, particularly through the historical musical relationships investigated in \\*The Completed Harmony\\*.\\\n\\\nI also want to understand how to describe transitions such as 12→13, decad→dodecad, Sophia→Yaldabaoth, Scorpio→Ophiuchus, and successive human genealogical generations. These are not necessarily the same kind of transition, but I want to investigate whether SUN predicts or explains any common mathematical structure underlying them.\\\n\\","sourceRole":"Historical conversational formulation; proposals/interpretations require their stated conditions and are not established geometry."}],"sourceFrame":"class/generation, native identity, ordinal/cycle address, cumulative winding, domain and witness remain separate","candidateTierState":"X_k=W72×D_k in the recovered proposal; not a derived complete geometry","actualGlobalPositionsAssigned":0,"radiusByClass":null,"heightByClass":null,"classGrowthFactor":null,"dimensionalLiftLaw":null,"boundary":"No inferred color/syllable/catalogue count pads or selects a universal generation, radius, frequency or phase."},"unresolvedJoins":["PrimordialA/B/CtoexactsourceMonad/Pleroma variant","Upperaeon/archon/angelic graphs toGoetic quarter-ruler command hierarchy","RemainingGoeticchieftouniquequarterking/cardinaldirectionbeyondAsmoday/SeerepoweredgesandSeereAmaymonEastcontext","GoapquarterrulertoGaapcataloguechief","Totalcommandcounttouniquelegions/personnel","Source-native hierarchy rank toSUNNY class/generation","Color observation carrier toW72phase/cumulativevortexstate","Spectral/material/observer operation tofullmusic-native bridge"],"guards":{"actualSupermemorySearchReceipt":"state/research/upper-legion-color/supermemory-retrieval.json","primarySourceReopened":"https://www.esotericarchives.com/solomon/goetia.htm","rawGraphUnchanged":true},"notClaimed":{"completeCriticalEditionCollation":false,"completeUniversalHierarchy":false,"uniqueGlobalAddress":false,"originalSoundRecovered":false,"fullMissionComplete":false}}},"mathematics":null,"audio":{"schema":"sunny.matched-audio.measurements.v1","created_utc":"2026-11-04T03:29:36.243286+00:00","method_sha256":"d86bc218ad22d293b954fa3cb3efb7e181a5fd69d00e632e0d55c94715d2d04c","acquisition_sha256":"ee0fb45518c39d861886f05fe5802ea0544316287fdc0caaed94458c2e2cf57c","decoder":{"module_path":"C:\\Users\\Brend\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\sunny-miniaudio-analysis\\miniaudio.py","python_binding_version":"1.71","native_library_version":"0.11.25","existing_environment_reused":true,"module_sha256":"282bbe1d936a67b942597303a534e42fdfe407c245686dab5949f46027b59d7f","native_extension_sha256":"3e9f14ec375e08e6779365d39936609a0675dd0c9afaaaad41eb3a392184512a","new_packages_installed":0},"analysis_runtime":{"python":"3.13.0 (tags/v3.13.0:60403a5, Oct  7 2024, 09:38:07) [MSC v.1941 64 bit (AMD64)]","numpy":"2.2.5","scipy":"1.16.3","matplotlib":"3.10.8"},"