name":"Original source assessments unchanged throughout calculation","status":"passed"},{"name":"Executed method follows actual Jev decision","status":"passed"}],"verdict":"proved as written for the stated mathematical model; linguistic application remains conditional on the source-qualified character states and evolutionary assumptions","labels":["Babylonian","Jerome","Palestinian","Secunda","Tiberian"],"states":{"derived1":["Babylonian","Tiberian"],"ancestral0":["Jerome","Palestinian","Secunda"]},"sourceFeature":{"id":"PW-C1","sourceLocator":"Chapter4 §2.1.1, pp77-79, Table9 on printed77/PDF90","sourceClaimStatus":"Author's proposed innovation and supporting argument inspected; underlying manuscript and external chronology claims not independently reproduced"},"sourceBindings":{"docs/reconstruction/symbol-sound-census/phyla-waves-assessment.json":"c64301e3db491f1978b490e0cfefaf7a4d6fd8ac484be58a031f79a49ff43bd3","docs/reconstruction/symbol-sound-census/reading-tradition-edge-assessment.json":"8e2968a1fd90071e65eaddc31f7bd3004914658094fac0ea83e67d25eb99a25a"},"treeConvention":"Fully resolved rooted non-plane binary trees; five distinct leaf labels; unlabelled internal nodes; no branch lengths, internal rankings, dates, contact edges or sampled ancestors.","primaryAssumptions":["Root/ancestral state0","Exactly one0-to1 innovation","No1-to0 loss","No contact, parallel origin or scribal mixing in this character","The five leaf states are treated as specified for this calculation, not independently proven historical observations"],"counts":{"unconstrained":105,"compatible":15,"excluded":90},"compatibleFractionOfSuppliedFamily":"1/7","fractionBoundary":"A combinatorial fraction, not a prior, posterior, calibrated confidence or probability of actual genealogy.","enumerators":{"rootBipartitions":105,"independentFixedLabelInsertion":105,"insertionStages":[{"leaves":1,"count":1},{"leaves":2,"count":1},{"leaves":3,"count":3},{"leaves":4,"count":15},{"leaves":5,"count":105}],"stateSolver":"All binary internal-node assignments with root0 tested for each topology; no-loss exactly-one-gain condition compared to explicit clade membership.","cladeCollapse":15},"proof":{"unconstrained":"A rooted binary tree on n-1 leaves has2n-4 edges plus one root-stem insertion position. Insert labelled leaf n at one of2n-3 positions. Deletion of that leaf and suppression of its parent is the unique inverse, so T1=1 and Tn=(2n-3)T(n-1). Therefore T5=1*3*5*7=105.","oneFeature":"With root0, one0-to1 gain and no loss, exactly the descendants below the gain are1. Hence the two1leaves must form a clade. Conversely any tree with that clade admits the gain on its entering edge, with all other states0.","compatible":"Collapse the fixed two-leaf clade to one label X. This bijects compatible five-leaf trees with arbitrary rooted binary trees on X and the other three labels. T4=1*3*5=15; the two-leaf expansion is unique.","independentFormula":"Fully labelled planar trees count C(n-1)*n!; exchanging the two children of each of n-1 internal nodes acts freely with distinct leaf labels. Quotient by2^(n-1). For n=5 this is14*120/16=105."},"onlyNontrivialCommonClade":["Babylonian","Tiberian"],"allCompatibleTreesNewick":["((((Babylonian,Tiberian),Jerome),Palestinian),Secunda);","((((Babylonian,Tiberian),Jerome),Secunda),Palestinian);","((((Babylonian,Tiberian),Palestinian),Jerome),Secunda);","((((Babylonian,Tiberian),Palestinian),Secunda),Jerome);","((((Babylonian,Tiberian),Secunda),Jerome),Palestinian);","((((Babylonian,Tiberian),Secunda),Palestinian),Jerome);","(((Babylonian,Tiberian),(Jerome,Palestinian)),Secunda);","(((Babylonian,Tiberian),(Jerome,Secunda)),Palestinian);","(((Babylonian,Tiberian),(Palestinian,Secunda)),Jerome);","(((Babylonian,Tiberian),Jerome),(Palestinian,Secunda));","(((Babylonian,Tiberian),Palestinian),(Jerome,Secunda));","(((Babylonian,Tiberian),Secunda),(Jerome,Palestinian));","(((Jerome,Palestinian),Secunda),(Babylonian,Tiberian));","(((Jerome,Sec